<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Grauholz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1798</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-invasion-of-switzerland">French invasion of Switzerland</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Grauholz was fought on 5 March 1798 north-east of Bern, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-invasion-of-switzerland">French invasion of Switzerland</a>. A French army under General Schauenburg defeated the Bernese forces, and the city of Bern surrendered the same day. The defeat brought down the Old Swiss Confederacy, which was replaced by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helvetic-republic">Helvetic Republic</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-grauholz.jpg" alt="Battle of Grauholz" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Weberschiffchen at German Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GrauholzWalthard_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
